Design: I will fine-tune the last convolutional block (layer4) and the fully‐connected head of ResNet50 end‐to‐end instead of using frozen features with LightGBM. I will replace the classifier head with a single‐output layer for binary malignancy prediction and apply BCEWithLogitsLoss with sample weights based on skin tone. I will train for 5 epochs per fold with StratifiedKFold cross‐validation, using simple augmentations (random horizontal flips and rotations). After printing the mean AUROC across folds, I'll retrain the full model on all data, save it, and provide a `predict()` function to load the saved model and compute malignancy probabilities for new images.
