Design: We can work around the unsupported `early_stopping_rounds` argument by using LightGBM’s callback interface. In the revised code, we replace `early_stopping_rounds` and `verbose_eval` with `callbacks=[lgb.callback.early_stopping(50), lgb.callback.log_evaluation(period=0)]`. We perform 5‐fold CV, collect AUCs and best iterations, and print the mean CV AUC. We then retrain on all data for 1.1× the average best iteration, save the model, and use a `predict()` function to generate and save a `submission.csv`.
