Design: I propose to enhance feature robustness by applying simple test‐time augmentation: for each image, we extract ViT features on both the original and a horizontally flipped version, then average these feature vectors. This TTA should reduce feature variance and improve classifier performance without significantly increasing runtime. We'll apply this in both cross‐validation and final predictions, updating the `extract_features` calls accordingly. The rest of the pipeline (5‐fold CV with LightGBM, retraining, saving model, and `predict()`) remains the same, now leveraging TTA‐averaged features.
